{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "חשן משפט", :translit "choshen mishpat", :gloss "breastplate of judgment"} {:he "מכפר על עונות משפט", :translit "mekhaper al avonot mishpat", :gloss "it atones for sins of judgment"} {:he "מה משפט ביום אף שאלת אורים ביום", :translit "mah mishpat ba-yom af she'elat urim ba-yom", :gloss "just as judgment is by day, so too inquiry of the Urim is by day"} {:he "בגימ' מכפר [על] הרהור הלב", :translit "be-gimatria mekhaper [al] hirhur ha-lev", :gloss "in gematria it atones [for] the musings of the heart"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "חשן משפט", :b "מכפר על הרהור הלב"}], :frame {:text "The high priest's breastplate (choshen) contained the Urim and Tummim, through which Israel could inquire of God (Exodus 28:30). The Torah stipulates that the breastplate is placed over Aaron's heart when he enters the sanctuary before God (Exodus 28:29–30). Yoma 73a discusses procedures for consulting the Urim, noting that the priest is enwrapped and asked the question, and raising the question of whether inquiry is permitted at night. Rashi on Exodus 28:30, citing the Sifre, identifies the choshen as atoning for miscarriages of justice. The phrase 'חשן משפט' as atoning for 'עונות משפט' follows this identification.", :sources ["Exodus 28:15" "Exodus 28:29–30" "Yoma 73a" "Rashi on Exodus 28:30" "Sifre Zuta 28:30"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "חשן משפט", :a-value 787, :b "מכפר על הרהור הלב", :b-value 893, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:19:50.939053171Z", :model "glm-5.2"}